    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1511">

                <pb facs="0974" n="858" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/159a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Letcher.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of complications that have arisen you will please await further
                    instructions before doing anything more in regard to the examination of Benton’s
                    body. Show this to Edwards, Cobb and Carothers so they may be likewise
                    informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
